\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c36\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>7</mn><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>36</mn></mrow></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td>\n                                </tr>\n                            </tbody></table> \n                              \n                    </div>",
  "text": "Question 8\nA calculator is required to answer the following question.\n\nA license plate has an ordered combination of \n7\n possible characters, as shown below:\n\nLetter or digit\tLetter or digit\tLetter or digit\tLetter or digit\tLetter or digit\tLetter or digit\tLetter or digit\n\nHere,\n\neach \"Letter\" can be any capital from A-Z (\n26\n in total), and\n\neach \"Digit\" can be any integer between \n0\n-\n9.\n\nHow many possible ordered combinations are there?\n\na\n\t\n26\n4\n×\n10\n3\n\n\nb\n\t\n26\n×\n10\n\n\nc\n\t\n36\n7\n\n\nd\n\t\n26\n3\n×\n10\n4\n\n\ne\n\t\n7\n36"
